#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "QUBO transformation {#qubo-transformation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From constraints to QUBO: the mathematical transformation {#from-"
"constraints-to-qubo-the-mathematical-transformation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The power of quantum optimization lies in transforming constrained problems "
"into unconstrained quadratic forms [\\[4\\]](#references). For the Market "
"Split problem, we convert the equality constraints\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$ Ax = b $$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where $x ∈ \\{0,1\\}^n$, into a QUBO by penalizing constraint violations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The penalty method:**\n"
"Since we need $Ax = b$ to hold exactly, we minimize the squared violation:\n"
"$$f(x) = ||Ax - b||^2$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This equals zero precisely when all constraints are satisfied. Expanding algebraically:\n"
"$$f(x) = (Ax - b)^T(Ax - b) = x^T A^T A x - 2b^T A x + b^T b$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**QUBO objective:**\n"
"Since $b^T b$ is constant, our optimization becomes:\n"
"$$\\text{minimize} \\quad Q(x) = x^T(A^T A)x - 2(A^T b)^T x$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key insight:** This transformation is exact, not approximate. Equality "
"constraints naturally square into quadratic form without requiring auxiliary"
" variables or penalty parameters - making this formulation mathematically "
"elegant and computationally efficient for quantum solvers "
"[\\[4\\]](#references). We'll use the `OptimizationProblem` class to define "
"our constrained problem, then convert it to QUBO format using "
"`OptimizationProblemToQubo`, both from the **qiskit_addon_opt_mapper** "
"package. This automatically handles the penalty-based transformation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Implement data loading and QUBO conversion functions {#implement-data-"
"loading-and-qubo-conversion-functions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now define three utility functions:\n"
"1. `parse_marketsplit_dat()` - Parses the `.dat` file format and extracts matrices $A$ and $b$\n"
"2. `fetch_marketsplit_data()` - Downloads problem instances directly from the QOBLIB repository\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Load the problem instance {#load-the-problem-instance}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we load the specific problem instance `ms_03_200_177.dat` from QOBLIB [2]. This instance has:\n"
"- 3 products (constraints)\n"
"- 20 markets (binary decision variables)\n"
"- Over 1 million possible market assignments to explore ($2^{20} = 1,048,576$)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Convert to QUBO format {#convert-to-qubo-format}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now transform the constrained optimization problem into QUBO format:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Convert QUBO to Iskay format {#convert-qubo-to-iskay-format}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we need to convert the QUBO object into the dictionary format required "
"by Kipu Quantum's Iskay Optimizer.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `problem` and `problem_type` arguments encode an optimization problem of"
" the form\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"\\min_{(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\in D} C(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
"where\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C(x_1, ... , x_n) = a + \\sum_{i} b_i x_i + \\sum_{i, j} c_{i, j} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum_{k_1, ..., k_m} g_{k_1, ..., k_m} x_{k_1} ... x_{k_m}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By choosing `problem_type = \"binary\"`, you specify that the cost function "
"is in `binary` format, which means that $D = \\{0,  1\\}^{n}$, as in, the "
"cost function is written in QUBO/HUBO formulation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, by choosing `problem_type = \"spin\"`, the cost function "
"is written in Ising formulation, where $D = \\{-1, 1\\}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The coefficients of the problem should be encoded in a dictionary as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align} \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\{} \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"()\"}&: \\quad &a, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i,)\"}&: \\quad &b_i, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i, j)\"}&: \\quad &c_{i, j}, \\quad (i \\neq j) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\quad  \\vdots \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(} k_1, ..., k_m  \\texttt{)\"}&: \\quad &g_{k_1, ..., k_m}, \\quad (k_1 \\neq k_2 \\neq \\dots \\neq k_m) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\}}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the keys of the dictionary must be strings containing a valid "
"tuple of non-repeating integers. For binary problems, we know that:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x_i^2 = x_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for $i=j$ (since $x_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$ means $x_i \\cdot x_i = x_i$). So, in "
"your QUBO formulation, if you have both linear contributions $b_i x_i$ and "
"diagonal quadratic contributions $c_{i,i} x_i^2$, these terms must be "
"combined into a single linear coefficient:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Total linear coefficient for variable $x_i$:** $b_i + c_{i,i}$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means:\n"
"- Linear terms like `\"(i, )\"` contain: original linear coefficient + diagonal quadratic coefficient\n"
"- Diagonal quadratic terms like `\"(i, i)\"` should **NOT** appear in the final dictionary\n"
"- Only off-diagonal quadratic terms like `\"(i, j)\"` where $i \\neq j$ should be included as separate entries\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example:** If your QUBO has $3x_1 + 2x_1^2 + 4x_1 x_2$, the Iskay dictionary should contain:\n"
"- `\"(0, )\"`: `5.0` (combining $3 + 2 = 5$)\n"
"- `\"(0, 1)\"`: `4.0` (off-diagonal term)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**NOT** separate entries for `\"(0, )\"`: `3.0` and `\"(0, 0)\"`: `2.0`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the bf-DCQO algorithm {#understand-the-bf-dcqo-algorithm}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we run the optimization, let's understand the sophisticated quantum "
"algorithm that powers Iskay: **bf-DCQO (bias-field digitized counterdiabatic"
" quantum optimization)** [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is bf-DCQO? {#what-is-bf-dcqo}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"bf-DCQO is based on the time evolution of a quantum system where the problem"
" solution is encoded in the **ground state** (lowest energy state) of the "
"final quantum Hamiltonian [\\[1\\]](#references). The algorithm addresses a "
"fundamental challenge in quantum optimization:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The challenge**: Traditional adiabatic quantum computing requires very "
"slow evolution to maintain ground state conditions according to the "
"adiabatic theorem. This demands increasingly deep quantum circuits as "
"problem complexity grows, leading to more gate operations and accumulated "
"errors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The solution**: bf-DCQO uses counterdiabatic protocols to enable rapid "
"evolution while maintaining ground state fidelity, dramatically reducing "
"circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical framework {#mathematical-framework}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The algorithm minimizes a cost function of the form:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\min_{(x_1,x_2,...,x_n) \\in D} C(x_1,x_2,...,x_n)$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where $D = \\{0,1\\}^n$ for binary variables and:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$C(x) = a + \\sum_i b_i x_i + \\sum_{i,j} c_{ij} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum "
"g_{k_1,...,k_m} x_{k_1}...x_{k_m}$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For our Market Split problem, the cost function is:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$C(x) = ||Ax - b||^2 = x^T A^T A x - 2 b^T A x + b^T b$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The role of counterdiabatic terms {#the-role-of-counterdiabatic-terms}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Counterdiabatic terms** are additional terms introduced into the time-"
"dependent Hamiltonian that suppress unwanted excitations during the quantum "
"evolution. Here's why they're crucial:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In adiabatic quantum optimization, we evolve the system according to a time-"
"dependent Hamiltonian:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$H(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t}{T}\\right) H_{\\text{initial}} + \\frac{t}{T} "
"H_{\\text{problem}}$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $H_{\\text{problem}}$ encodes our optimization problem. To maintain "
"the ground state during rapid evolution, we add counterdiabatic terms:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$H_{\\text{CD}}(t) = H(t) + H_{\\text{counter}}(t)$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These counterdiabatic terms do the following:\n"
"1. **Suppress unwanted transitions**: Prevent the quantum state from jumping to excited states during fast evolution\n"
"2. **Enable shorter evolution times**: Allow us to reach the final state much faster without violating adiabaticity\n"
"3. **Reduce circuit depth**: Shorter evolution leads to fewer gates and less error\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The practical impact is dramatic: bf-DCQO uses up to **10 times fewer "
"entangling gates** than Digital Quantum Annealing [\\[1\\]](#references), "
"making it practical for today's noisy quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bias-field iterative optimization {#bias-field-iterative-optimization}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unlike variational algorithms that optimize circuit parameters through many "
"iterations, bf-DCQO uses a **bias-field guided approach** that converges in "
"approximately 10 iterations [1]:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Iteration process:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Initial quantum evolution**: Start with a quantum circuit implementing the"
" counterdiabatic evolution protocol\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Measurement**: Measure the quantum state to obtain a probability "
"distribution over bitstrings\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Bias-field calculation**: Analyze the measurement statistics and calculate an optimal bias-field $h_i$ for each qubit:\n"
"$$h_i = \\text{f}(\\text{measurement statistics}, \\text{previous solutions})$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Next iteration**: The bias-field modifies the Hamiltonian for the next iteration:\n"
"$$H_{\\text{next}} = H_{\\text{problem}} + \\sum_i h_i \\sigma_i^z$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   This allows starting near the previously found good solution, effectively"
" performing a form of \"quantum local search\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Convergence**: Repeat until the solution quality stabilizes or a maximum "
"number of iterations is reached\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key advantage**: Each iteration provides meaningful progress toward the "
"optimal solution by incorporating information from previous measurements, "
"unlike variational methods that must explore the parameter space blindly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Integrated classical post-processing {#integrated-classical-post-processing}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After the quantum optimization converges, Iskay performs classical **local "
"search** post-processing:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Bit-flip exploration**: Systematically or randomly flip bits in the best "
"measured solution\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Energy evaluation**: Calculate $C(x)$ for each modified solution\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Greedy selection**: Accept improvements that lower the cost function\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Multiple passes**: Perform several passes (controlled by "
"`postprocessing_level`)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This hybrid approach compensates for bit-flip errors from hardware "
"imperfections and readout errors, ensuring high-quality solutions even on "
"noisy quantum devices.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Why bf-DCQO excels on current hardware {#why-bf-dcqo-excels-on-current-"
"hardware}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bf-DCQO algorithm is specifically designed to excel on today's noisy "
"intermediate-scale quantum (NISQ) devices [\\[1\\]](#references):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Error resilience**: Fewer gates (10 times reduction) means dramatically "
"less error accumulation\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**No error mitigation required**: The algorithm's inherent efficiency "
"eliminates the need for expensive error mitigation techniques "
"[\\[1\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Scalability**: Can handle problems with up to 156 qubits (156 binary "
"variables) with direct qubit-mapping [\\[1\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Proven performance**: Achieves 100% approximation ratios on benchmark "
"MaxCut and HUBO instances [\\[1\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's see this powerful algorithm in action on our Market Split "
"problem!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bf-DCQO algorithm automatically handles circuit optimization, creating "
"shallow quantum circuits with counterdiabatic terms specifically designed "
"for the target backend.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Configure the optimization {#configure-the-optimization}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Iskay Optimizer requires several key parameters to effectively solve "
"your optimization problem. Let's examine each parameter and its role in the "
"quantum optimization process:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Required parameters {#required-parameters}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Parameter | Type | Description | Example |\n"
"|-----------|------|-------------|---------|\n"
"| **problem** | `Dict[str, float]` | QUBO coefficients in string-key format | `{\"()\": -21.0, \"(0,4)\": 0.5, \"(0,1)\": 0.5}` |\n"
"| **problem_type** | `str` | Format specification: `\"binary\"` for QUBO or `\"spin\"` for Ising | `\"binary\"` |\n"
"| **backend_name** | `str` | Target quantum device | `\"ibm_fez\"` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Essential concepts {#essential-concepts}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Problem format**: We use `\"binary\"` since our variables are binary "
"(0/1), representing market assignments.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Backend selection**: Choose between the available QPUs (for example, "
"`\"ibm_fez\"`) based on your needs and compute resource instance.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**QUBO structure**: Our problem dictionary contains the exact coefficients "
"from the mathematical transformation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Advanced options (optional) {#advanced-options-optional}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Iskay provides fine-tuning capabilities through optional parameters. While "
"the defaults work well for most problems, you can customize the behavior for"
" specific requirements:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n"
"|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n"
"| **shots** | `int` | 10000 | Quantum measurements per iteration (higher = more accurate) |\n"
"| **num_iterations** | `int` | 10 | Algorithm iterations (more iterations can improve solution quality) |\n"
"| **use_session** | `bool` | True | Use IBM sessions for reduced queue times |\n"
"| **seed_transpiler** | `int` | None | Set for reproducible quantum circuit compilation |\n"
"| **direct_qubit_mapping** | `bool` | False | Map virtual qubits directly to physical qubits |\n"
"| **job_tags** | `List[str]` | None | Custom tags for job tracking |\n"
"| **preprocessing_level** | `int` | 0 | Problem preprocessing intensity (0-3) - see details below |\n"
"| **postprocessing_level** | `int` | 2 | Solution refinement level (0-2) - see details below |\n"
"| **transpilation_level** | `int` | 0 | Transpiler optimization trials (0-5) - see details below |\n"
"| **transpile_only** | `bool` | False | Analyze circuit optimization without running full execution |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Preprocessing Levels (0-3)**: Specially important for larger problems that cannot currently fit on the coherence times of the hardware. Higher preprocessing levels achieve shallower circuit depths by approximations in the problem transpilation:\n"
"- **Level 0**: Exact, longer circuits\n"
"- **Level 1**: Good balance between accuracy and approximation, cutting out only the gates with angles in the lowest 10 percentile\n"
"- **Level 2**: Slightly higher approximation, cutting out the gates with angles in the lowest 20 percentile and using `approximation_degree=0.95` in the transpilation\n"
"- **Level 3**: Maximum approximation level, cutting out the gates in the lowest 30 percentile and using `approximation_degree=0.90` in the transpilation\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Transpilation Levels (0-5)**: Control the advanced transpiler optimization trials for quantum circuit compilation. This can lead to an increase in classical overhead, and for some cases it might not change the circuit depth. The default value `2` in general leads to the smallest circuit and is relatively fast.\n"
"- **Level 0**: Optimization of the decomposed DCQO circuit (layout, routing, scheduling)\n"
"- **Level 1**: Optimization of `PauliEvolutionGate` and then the decomposed DCQO circuit (max_trials=10)\n"
"- **Level 2**: Optimization of `PauliEvolutionGate` and then the decomposed DCQO circuit (max_trials=15)\n"
"- **Level 3**: Optimization of `PauliEvolutionGate` and then the decomposed DCQO circuit (max_trials=20)\n"
"- **Level 4**: Optimization of `PauliEvolutionGate` and then the decomposed DCQO circuit (max_trials=25)\n"
"- **Level 5**: Optimization of `PauliEvolutionGate` and then the decomposed DCQO circuit (max_trials=50)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Postprocessing Levels (0-2)**: Control how much classical optimization, compensating for bit-flip errors with different number of greedy passes of a local search:\n"
"- **Level 0**: 1 pass\n"
"- **Level 1**: 2 passes\n"
"- **Level 2**: 3 passes\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Transpile-only mode**: Now available for users who want to analyze circuit"
" optimization without running the full quantum algorithm execution.\n"
msgstr ""

